    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0274" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 184.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 181, of June 29,
                    inclosing a copy of my dispatch transmitting to the minister of foreign affairs
                    the expression of the sympathies of the American people and Government, I now
                    send a copy and translation of Mr. Hanotaux’s reply to the same.</p>
                <p>I also inclose a copy of your telegram received June 30, informing me that the
                    President, Cabinet, members of the Senate and House of Representatives would
                    attend on Sunday a religious service at Washington in memory of the late
                    President, which information was at once communicated to Mr. Hanotaux.</p>
                <p>I add a copy of my telegram of the 2d instant relative to the funeral of
                    President Carnot, for which I ordered a large wreath, which I sent to the Palais
                    de I’Élysée.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Eustis.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d213-a1.xml" xpointer="d213-a1"/>
            </div>
